{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope","id":1193313,"title":"The Time Traveler's Microscope","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T14:38:32-08:00","id":1193313,"title":"The Time Traveler's Microscope","content":"Through use of Time, a Mage travels back to the 1100s. They bring a single microscope. Taking some infected sample from a sick person, they make a slide and examine it under high magnification.<br /> <br /> Now, Mage STs; what do they see?<br /> <br /> - They see organic pathogens such as bacteria, since those have always existed and always been the vector of disease. This has serious ramifications; it means that Sleepers do not warp reality, and it means that the universe assumes a certain &quot;objective shape&quot; without outside influence. It means that Sleepers simply shape the Consensus, and all that does is affect whether Magick is vulgar or not, making it easier or harder to reshape things. So the Mage who thinks that &quot;bad air&quot; spreads illness is wrong, and his paradigm is loose and fluffy compared to the more &quot;real&quot; paradigm of a Technocrat bioterrorist who has an intimate understanding of what actually causes disease, up to the point where she could spread disease without Magick if she needed to.<br /> <br /> - They see no evidence of pathogenic microorganisms. Instead, they are able to detect a General Aura Of Badness. This &quot;Stuff&quot; is diseased stuff (imbalanced humours, miasma, malaise), and it will make people diseased. How? Good question! Now this wouldn't be unreasonable, since the books seem to flip-flop between &quot;collective thought shapes reality&quot; and &quot;collective thought shapes the way that Magick shapes reality&quot;. If it's the former, than our Time Traveler will never see bacteria before the paradigm shift of the 1800s which embraced germ theory.<br /> <br /> The answer to this question is quite pertinent, and has ramifications. Do mobile phones only work because of the Technocracy shaping the consensus until phones were just part of reality? The Mage books often lean on this being true, and have reality zones where such devices are less reliable. Or are mobile phones just something that is an application of the basic nature of reality, fundamental physical behavior?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-08-2018, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:35:58-08:00","id":1193330,"title":"","content":"Would the microscope even work? I'm not sure that it would.<br /> <br /> In mage, using a microscope would sort of be like a Life 1 rote under the technocratic paradigm, which even sleepers would be capable of using since it is a part of the consensus.<br /> <br /> If, however, we were back in a time where there was no such consensus, then the use of a microscope would be just as magical as hitting sticks together to drive away the spirits.<br /> If the mage had a paradigm which allowed for the microscope to work, i.e. they believed that light can be reflected and bent via ocular lenses so as to magnify an image, and thus can be used to allow us to see that which is smaller than can be seen by the eye alone, then they would be able to use the microscope for their Life 1 spell.<br /> <br /> But what they see down the microscope will also depend entirely on their paradigm. Perhaps they see little demons or spirits moving around the blood, Perhaps they see small kingdoms at war. Or perhaps instead they see shapes, pure mathematical shapes, or the forms that Plato described. Or even bacteria, so long as that is what they expect to see.<br /> Without consensus on how this tool works, there is also no consensus on what would be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-09-2018, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:13:31-08:00","id":1193377,"title":"","content":"You'd see bacteria because the microscope exists as part of a particular paradigm it cannot detect bad humours or chi imbalance or Disease spirits(which are also still there in modern times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T03:32:17-08:00","id":1193478,"title":"","content":"An alternative suggestion: I don't think it would become a mere practice-tool that is dependant on the paradigm of the awakened/enlightend user. I think it would become a simple wonder!<br /> <br /> Since the microscope, upon traveling back in time, becomes something that has very defined abilities that are not part of the consentual reality it accordingly becomes full-blown sphere-magickal - as that is pretty much the definition of anything outside of full consensus.<br /> <br /> That is, it turns (back) into a wonder of the Talisman, Trinket or Device type, since those are usable by anybody.<br /> Not a high-quality wonder probably because of mass-production and no big personal investment, but a simple Forces 2 (Maybe with Corr 2) based one-trick pony which would also be affected by paradox as soon as a sleeper gazes through it.<br /> <br /> And, according to the paradigm the microscope-wonder was created under, it would always show cells and such for everybody gazing through.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-09-2018, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T03:57:31-08:00","id":1193484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193330#post1193330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the microscope even work? I'm not sure that it would.<br /> <br /> In mage, using a microscope would sort of be like a Life 1 rote under the technocratic paradigm, which even sleepers would be capable of using since it is a part of the consensus.<br /> <br /> If, however, we were back in a time where there was no such consensus, then the use of a microscope would be just as magical as hitting sticks together to drive away the spirits.<br /> If the mage had a paradigm which allowed for the microscope to work, i.e. they believed that light can be reflected and bent via ocular lenses so as to magnify an image, and thus can be used to allow us to see that which is smaller than can be seen by the eye alone, then they would be able to use the microscope for their Life 1 spell.<br /> <br /> But what they see down the microscope will also depend entirely on their paradigm. Perhaps they see little demons or spirits moving around the blood, Perhaps they see small kingdoms at war. Or perhaps instead they shapes, pure mathematical shapes, or the forms that Plato described. Or even bacteria, so long as that is what they expect to see.<br /> Without consensus on how this tool works, there is also no consensus on what would be seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But such a suggestion completely ruins scientific history.<br /> <br /> A person believes something that goes against the consensus of the learned world, as well as common wisdom. And yet they are able to demonstrate that they are correct, in a reproducible manner. They aren't some victor in the so-called &quot;marketplace of ideas&quot; (ugh), they win because no matter how stubborn other learned people are, they have some way of demonstrating that they are correct. John Snow was able to show others that germ theory was correct, while the absolute consensus in his reality zone was Miasma spreading disease. Was he insane? Was he warping reality to suit his own theories? Was the paradigm shift some grand application of Mind?<br /> <br /> If we follow the answer that technology relies on belief, that our microscope works because of Consensus (fully correct within the Mage Lore, but frequently contradicted from what I can see), then John Snow was wrong. Disease was being spread by Miasma, and all of the methods being used to counter this spread were correct. But when we look at attempts to prevent the spread of disease through scented smoke, cleansing the city of dirt, things just got worse, in a way that doesn't match the paradigm.<br /> <br /> Consensus: dirt in the city is releasing a miasma.<br /> Idea: we can fix that by pushing all of the dirt into the river and letting the city wash itself of the impurity.<br /> Consensual Result: people stop dying of cholera<br /> Actual Result, which defies Consensus: it gets worse, because despite the consensus, cholera was spread by a germ, not by bad air.<br /> <br /> See the problem?<br /> <br /> And how about a modern example? Shills for the sugar industry convinced everyone that fat makes you fat. That's consensual, thanks to mass marketing. Ask people what kind of food makes you fat, and fatty foods are an obvious answer. The real answer is that we produce fat most efficiently when we have excess glucose in our system, and this can be proven metabolically and by looking at the dangerous results of people cutting fat out of their diets, eating &quot;healthy&quot; zero-fat alternatives which have been packed with sugar to fix the awful taste. If Consensus really shapes reality, then low-fat foods would make people more thin. The opposite is true, sadly. And how about the old consensus of cigarettes being good for you? Or radiation being good for you? If the consensus is actively shaping reality in such powerful ways as allowing mobile phones to work, then what's going on here?<br /> <br /> My head-canon (which the Mage books do seem to occasionally use, as this isn't super well thought out) is that Consensus is only relevant when it comes to Magick. The Technocrats shape the Consensus to make enlightened procedures less paradoxical, and to make &quot;Magick&quot; more paradoxical. Sleepers might think that cigarettes help you get over chest infections, and this might make a disease-curing cigar Coincidental, but that's all it does. Sleepers might think that low-fat foods help you loose weight (ignoring sugar), and this might make a nutritious zero-fat broth an effective &quot;potion&quot; a Mage could create to bring about weight loss, but this doesn't mean that low-fat diets are good for you. Sleepers might think that a hit to the head can knock someone out for hours, reliably, Hollywood action movie style, and this might make it easier for a Mage to do this and make it Coincidental (a bit of Life and Time?), but it doesn't actually change the way a normal hit to the head works.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-09-2018, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:21:50-08:00","id":1193492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193484#post1193484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But such a suggestion completely ruins scientific history.<br /> <br /> A person believes something that goes against the consensus of the learned world, as well as common wisdom. And yet they are able to demonstrate that they are correct, in a reproducible manner. They aren't some victor in the so-called &quot;marketplace of ideas&quot; (ugh), they win because no matter how stubborn other learned people are, they have some way of demonstrating that they are correct. John Snow was able to show others that germ theory was correct, while the absolute consensus in his reality zone was Miasma spreading disease. Was he insane? Was he warping reality to suit his own theories? Was the paradigm shift some grand application of Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are some how under the impression there is One truth. There is not. Its not Miasma theory OR germ theory are right. They are both are true at the same time. Germ Theory has proven to be a more effective Paradigm in the ultimate treatment of disease so Miasma theory was discarded by the Order of Reason. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:43:00-08:00","id":1193494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193484#post1193484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But such a suggestion completely ruins scientific history.<br /> <br /> &lt;Stuff&gt;<br /> <br /> See the problem?<br /> <br /> &lt;More stuff!&gt;<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does! - but it essentially is another part of the &quot;All of reality is subjective&quot; vs &quot;Reality is mostly subjective except for Earthly Foundations&quot; vs &quot;Most of reality is part of Earthly Foundations&quot; argument. Or rather than argument, I probably should say &quot;Basic options for your Mage game to pick from&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think if you take the Mage default of &quot;Reality mostly subjective except Earthly Foundations&quot;, you shouldn't take our current known RL history as what actually happened - what's written would already differ some in the World Of Darkness baseline, and divert further in a default Mage-specific game.<br /> <br /> <br /> First and foremost, history is written by the victor, and you can bet that the Order of Reason and later the Technocracy have moved every lever they could in order to have their 'approved' version of history taught and in the books. &quot;Look at that John Snow, thinking that it was dirt miasma. Ha ha, what a fool.&quot;<br /> Heck, rewriting history is actually literally one of the core disciplines and efforts of the NWO. And it starts right there in the history books.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second, and going straight for your example of modern times and the effects of diets, I don't think you can call very specific statements like 'fat food makes you fat' something that is actually a firm part of the overall consensus.<br /> There are so many people constantly arguing about diets, new studies being released, and so many different 'exceptions', that I think the actual consensus is a lower baseline that everybody agrees on: &quot;Eating too much makes you fat.&quot; Everybody agrees on that, but the more you go into details, the more arguments you'll get.<br /> The consensus is really only firm along such baselines that people don't argue about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:55:56-08:00","id":1193499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193494#post1193494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does! - but it essentially is another part of the &quot;All of reality is subjective&quot; vs &quot;Reality is mostly subjective except for Earthly Foundations&quot; vs &quot;Most of reality is part of Earthly Foundations&quot; argument. Or rather than argument, I probably should say &quot;Basic options for your Mage game to pick from&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I wonder if the Mage books are up-front enough about this? If I were editing M20, I would put this at the forefront of discussions on Magick, as it's a pretty big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:01:48-08:00","id":1193501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193492#post1193492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are some how under the impression there is One truth. There is not. Its not Miasma theory OR germ theory are right. They are both are true at the same time. Germ Theory has proven to be a more effective Paradigm in the ultimate treatment of disease so Miasma theory was discarded by the Order of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is just empty rhetoric though. &quot;They're both true simultaneously&quot; doesn't hold water when you consider that every assumption based around Miasma theory was wrong (except for the tangential connection between miasma and airborne pathogens, which is in fact just part of Germ theory which Miasma theory imitates through chance). Either it's a recorded fact that there were huge cholera outbreaks when people pushed all of the Miasma-producing materials of London into the Thames, or it isn't.<br /> <br /> Now you could go very meta and say that all of the information we have on this has been filtered through the NWO, that Miasma-related treatment actually did work and stopped working when the OoR discarded it for another theory (seemingly for no reason; if it ain't broke, don't fix it), and that since then history has been censored to make pre-germ doctors look like morons in treating infectious disease. But at that point, I don't think you have WoD. I'm okay with Rasputin secretly being a Mage or a Vampire, for instance, or the enlightenment in Science in the 20th century having been the birth of the Technocracy, but the vast vast vast majority of our history simply being inaccurate because of the control of the honest-to-god Illuminati? Nah. That isn't &quot;our world, but more corrupt and with supernatural creatures at the edges, hiding from mortal eyes&quot;, that's a straight-up Urban Fantasy World which only superficially resembles our own.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the NWO WISHES it had that kind of power. The NWO is fighting very hard to gain more control over the world, and has to pick its battles. It isn't in total control of established historical record, even if it is more powerful than most governments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-09-2018, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:06:05-08:00","id":1193503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But such a suggestion completely ruins scientific history.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can't abide that! Let's call NWO <i>immediately</i>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:09:57-08:00","id":1193505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193501#post1193501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is just empty rhetoric though. &quot;They're both true simultaneously&quot; doesn't hold water when you consider that every assumption based around Miasma theory was wrong (except for the tangential connection between miasma and airborne pathogens, which is in fact just part of Germ theory which Miasma theory imitates through chance). Either it's a recorded fact that there were huge cholera outbreaks when people pushed all of the Miasma-producing materials of London into the Thames, or it isn't.<br /> <br /> Now you could go very meta and say that all of the information we have on this has been filtered through the NWO, that Miasma-related treatment actually did work and stopped working when the OoR discarded it for another theory (seemingly for no reason; if it ain't broke, don't fix it), and that since then history has been censored to make pre-germ doctors look like morons in treating infectious disease. But at that point, I don't think you have WoD. I'm okay with Rasputin secretly being a Mage or a Vampire, for instance, or the enlightenment in Science in the 20th century having been the birth of the Technocracy, but the vast vast vast majority of our history simply being inaccurate because of the control of the honest-to-god Illuminati? Nah. That isn't &quot;our world, but more corrupt and with supernatural creatures at the edges, hiding from mortal eyes&quot;, that's a straight-up Urban Fantasy World which only superficially resembles our own.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the NWO WISHES it had that kind of power. The NWO is fighting very hard to gain more control over the world, and has to pick its battles. It isn't in total control of established historical record, even if it is more powerful than most governments.</div> </div> </div> </div>You made a thread about this already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mage it's very meta. You have Etherites leaving because Tychoides choosed he wanted empty space out the athmosphere. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:12:38-08:00","id":1193509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193505#post1193505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You made a thread about this already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mage it's very meta. You have Etherites leaving because Tychoides choosed he wanted empty space out the athmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think about a year back I raised these problems in an existing thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:21:22-08:00","id":1193511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope#post1193313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through use of Time, a Mage travels back to the 1100s. They bring a single microscope. Taking some infected sample from a sick person, they make a slide and examine it under high magnification.<br /> <br /> Now, Mage STs; what do they see?<br /> <br /> - They see organic pathogens such as bacteria, since those have always existed and always been the vector of disease. This has serious ramifications; it means that Sleepers do not warp reality, and it means that the universe assumes a certain &quot;objective shape&quot; without outside influence. It means that Sleepers simply shape the Consensus, and all that does is affect whether Magick is vulgar or not, making it easier or harder to reshape things. So the Mage who thinks that &quot;bad air&quot; spreads illness is wrong, and his paradigm is loose and fluffy compared to the more &quot;real&quot; paradigm of a Technocrat bioterrorist who has an intimate understanding of what actually causes disease, up to the point where she could spread disease without Magick if she needed to.<br /> <br /> - They see no evidence of pathogenic microorganisms. Instead, they are able to detect a General Aura Of Badness. This &quot;Stuff&quot; is diseased stuff (imbalanced humours, miasma, malaise), and it will make people diseased. How? Good question! Now this wouldn't be unreasonable, since the books seem to flip-flop between &quot;collective thought shapes reality&quot; and &quot;collective thought shapes the way that Magick shapes reality&quot;. If it's the former, than our Time Traveler will never see bacteria before the paradigm shift of the 1800s which embraced germ theory.<br /> <br /> The answer to this question is quite pertinent, and has ramifications. Do mobile phones only work because of the Technocracy shaping the consensus until phones were just part of reality? The Mage books often lean on this being true, and have reality zones where such devices are less reliable. Or are mobile phones just something that is an application of the basic nature of reality, fundamental physical behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Mage were to look through it, there's a good argument to be made that the idea of the microscope is embedded enough in their paradigm and practices to work, even if they aren't based in science. At that point he'd see whatever he expected to see, likely germs but possibly something else. If anyone else looked through it, it would probably not work, but it would do so in a way consistent with the problems with a microscope. Most likely I'd have it be almost impossible to get good resolution because the accuracy of the gears was impossible at that time. If a technically inclined Mage of the time had a mechanical paradigm that somehow worked with a modern microscope they would be able to see through it, but they would see whatever biology their paradigm says they should. <br /> <br /> As a side note, I seem to remember you going down this road before. Specifically the part about the cholera epidemic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:25:02-08:00","id":1193514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193511#post1193511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, I seem to remember you going down this road before. Specifically the part about the cholera epidemic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only using it because it's a good example of the scientific consensus being wrong in quite a tangible way, i.e. a preventative measure led to a rise in deaths because their paradigm misunderstood what they were trying to stop. I'm sure there are lots of other good examples, and I've mentioned a few (tabacco products and radiation), but none that I know as much about or can explain as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:28:55-08:00","id":1193517,"title":"","content":"As for the Microscope working/not working, that is whether the device would be able to show things at high resolution and with focus, regardless of whether bacteria (or other causes of disease) are present... if the microscope is a useless do-dad in the past, as the paradigms of the world haven't shifted to allow for precise machinery and all that is needed to make it work, then would that mean that stuff like the way light interacts with glass isn't part of the Earthly Foundations? Have fundamental physical properties changed so dramatically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:34:46-08:00","id":1193519,"title":"","content":"There isn't a canonical answer to your question, albeit I agree with Lian - Microscope was made with the idea to see bacteria in mind, if it works at all it's going to see bacteria. If this it's caused by a magickal effect, a Paradigm bubble brought through the time stream, objective reality (be it science or Gaia), or the Mage itself with her 20th century mindset, only the ST knows.<br /> <br /> Then again, a good argument could be made about Paradox tampering with any mundane future technology you bring through the timestream (it doesn't belong to this era, what a Paradox!). Another good argument could be made about the microscope just not working outside it's Consensus. So, it's entirely up the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> then would that mean that stuff like the way light interacts with glass isn't part of the Earthly Foundations? Have fundamental physical properties changed so dramatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. The consequences of those laws are not as obvious as you think - perhaps little dwarves cause earth attraction, perhaps fae control how light interacts with glass. Perhaps Paradox just wanted to be a bitch and your ST said &quot;it doesn't work&quot; without thinking about the objectivity/subjectivity axis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2018, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:43:44-08:00","id":1193521,"title":"","content":"Also, I think it needs to be stated that while the Earthly Foundations establish a certain set of very simple basic ground rules (Stuff falls down, fire is hot, honey badgers don't give a shit), the Earthly Foundations don't have it specified anywhere in the books *why* those rules are how they are.<br /> <br /> Fire will always be hot in normal consentual reality, but the Earthly Foundations don't specify wether that's because of particle motions or fire elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:45:39-08:00","id":1193523,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Gravity is a constant because it has pretty obvious effects. The way light interacts with glass isn't as obvious, I for one, not knowing physics, can't fathom the consequences of this set of fundamental physical properties being changed so dramatically. I imagine most people won't notice unless you chain this idea with other phenomena that should change if this particular law changes. Which would be a fallacy, the fallacy of the affirmation of the consequent (you would be doing science backwards, from the conclusions to the phenomena).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2018, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:46:47-08:00","id":1193524,"title":"","content":"That all makes sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> Do any of the Editions of Mage go into more depth on the Earthly Foundations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:54:13-08:00","id":1193530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193517#post1193517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Microscope working/not working, that is whether the device would be able to show things at high resolution and with focus, regardless of whether bacteria (or other causes of disease) are present... if the microscope is a useless do-dad in the past, as the paradigms of the world haven't shifted to allow for precise machinery and all that is needed to make it work, then would that mean that stuff like the way light interacts with glass isn't part of the Earthly Foundations? Have fundamental physical properties changed so dramatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>But it matters a great deal why it is a useless doodad in the past. You mention how light interacts with glass, but that's not the major problem in the 1100s. Ibn al-Haytham had already written his treatise on optics a century before, and most of it was never overturned. That doesn't mean that a adjustable focus lens system was possible in the century you chose but the principles behind it were more advanced than the other parts of the microscope or any kind of biological theory it could examine.<br /> <br /> Edit: I never appeal to Earthly Foundations if I can help it, so I left them out of my response, but everyone else has done a really good job of covering them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-09-2018, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:07:47-08:00","id":1193536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193530#post1193530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it matters a great deal why it is a useless doodad in the past. You mention how light interacts with glass, but that's not the major problem in the 1100s. Ibn al-Haytham had already written his treatise on optics a century before, and most of it was never overturned. That doesn't mean that a adjustable focus lens system was possible in the century you chose but the principles behind it were more advanced than the other parts of the microscope or any kind of biological theory it could examine.<br /> <br /> Edit: I never appeal to Earthly Foundations if I can help it, so I left them out of my response, but everyone else has done a really good job of covering them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting point that was also discussed in the past. &quot;If every property that composes a thing it's Consensual, shouldn't the composite thing work too?&quot;. This adds a twist in that the base of reality it's Consensual, but it can be built uppon.<br /> <br /> Fireweapons were Vulgar when Craftmasons first used them in Europe, but powder and fireworks were already invented ... in China. Maybe it was possible to build mundane fire weapons in China with the right know-how and tools (I mean, more &quot;modern&quot; fire weapons that what they already had at that time).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Do any of the Editions of Mage go into more depth on the Earthly Foundations?</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge. Revised had them as Universal Constants, but they weren't really more than a sidebar.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's for the best, as you CAN say that germs, like vampires and the Triad :P , always existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2018, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:31:11-08:00","id":1193544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193524#post1193524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of the Editions of Mage go into more depth on the Earthly Foundations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think M20 has the most detailed writeup - page 612 + 613. But even that isn't really...detailed. It has several examples though, and while it reaffirms that the Earthly Foundations cannot be broken, it also gives example how they can be slightly 'bent' with a lot of time and investment. Just a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:31:23-08:00","id":1193545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193536#post1193536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting point that was also discussed in the past. &quot;If every property that composes a thing it's Consensual, shouldn't the composite thing work too?&quot;. This adds a twist in that the base of reality it's Consensual, but it can be built uppon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would depend by what you mean by every. Those properties interacting in a predictable way would also be a property, whether or not you include that property drastically changes the question. In general, I would say that once all the properties (excluding the one about them all working together) are in place, the combination of them becomes possible. However, it's not always obvious what all the properties are. One of the things you see a lot in the history of technology is that even when people believe things are possible there can still be major problems getting them to work. Often things like precision and metallurgy can hold inventions back for decades, centuries, or (as in the case of the steam engine) millenia.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:06:51-08:00","id":1193609,"title":"","content":"They'd see bacteria or whatever they expect. Because they expect to see this. Magical practices work because the mage thinks they work and they will only ever work that way the mage expects them to behave. Well, sort of. It might get vulgar if the Microscope-Mage would show his &quot;invention&quot; to others but Paradox wasn't that big back then.<br /> Time related Paradox however would f*** him up, badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T22:16:49-08:00","id":1193815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193501#post1193501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is just empty rhetoric though. &quot;They're both true simultaneously&quot; doesn't hold water when you consider that every assumption based around Miasma theory was wrong (except for the tangential connection between miasma and airborne pathogens, which is in fact just part of Germ theory which Miasma theory imitates through chance). Either it's a recorded fact that there were huge cholera outbreaks when people pushed all of the Miasma-producing materials of London into the Thames, or it isn't.<br /> <br /> Now you could go very meta and say that all of the information we have on this has been filtered through the NWO, that Miasma-related treatment actually did work and stopped working when the OoR discarded it for another theory (seemingly for no reason; if it ain't broke, don't fix it), and that since then history has been censored to make pre-germ doctors look like morons in treating infectious disease. But at that point, I don't think you have WoD. I'm okay with Rasputin secretly being a Mage or a Vampire, for instance, or the enlightenment in Science in the 20th century having been the birth of the Technocracy, but the vast vast vast majority of our history simply being inaccurate because of the control of the honest-to-god Illuminati? Nah. That isn't &quot;our world, but more corrupt and with supernatural creatures at the edges, hiding from mortal eyes&quot;, that's a straight-up Urban Fantasy World which only superficially resembles our own.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the NWO WISHES it had that kind of power. The NWO is fighting very hard to gain more control over the world, and has to pick its battles. It isn't in total control of established historical record, even if it is more powerful than most governments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Miasma theory DOES work. If you are a mage. Humors Theory DOES work. If you are a mage. They even work if you are a Hedge Mage. Miasma as a Theory is a SHIT theory, its harder to impliment or do much with. So the OOR looked for a new theory they could more readily use to improve the human condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T13:41:21-08:00","id":1194025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193815#post1193815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Miasma theory DOES work. If you are a mage. Humors Theory DOES work. If you are a mage. They even work if you are a Hedge Mage. Miasma as a Theory is a SHIT theory, its harder to impliment or do much with. So the OOR looked for a new theory they could more readily use to improve the human condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes of course it works if you're a mage. You can make something akin to an atomic bomb with &quot;psionic waves&quot; if you're an Archmage.<br /> <br /> The question is whether Miasma ever was a real thing. Back when most people thought &quot;foul vapours&quot; spread disease... did they spread disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T13:55:56-08:00","id":1194029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1194025#post1194025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes of course it works if you're a mage. You can make something akin to an atomic bomb with &quot;psionic waves&quot; if you're an Archmage.<br /> <br /> The question is whether Miasma ever was a real thing. Back when most people thought &quot;foul vapours&quot; spread disease... did they spread disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>Miasma is as real as spirits<br /> <br /> Perhaps miasma is what humans sensed when the banes were about.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it\u2019s the other way round, and the smells created the spirits in response to human association.<br /> <br /> Hey, why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-10-2018, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:51:03-08:00","id":1194051,"title":"","content":"Yes Miasma is a real thing. As is chi imbalance, essential Humours, Bacteria, diseases demons etc.<br /> <br /> People don't believe in &quot;bacteria&quot; or miasma. They believe in &quot;medicine&quot; or &quot;sanitation&quot;. In mage John Snow creates an elaborate wonder known as &quot;London Sewers&quot; these make it so people are less likely to die of cholera. He then explains it as bacteria. But that doesn't matter what matters is people believe in Sanitation. People believe in outcomes not theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T06:14:57-07:00","id":1196773,"title":"","content":"The simple answer is that the mage sees various pathogens. Because that is the reality he knows. A modern mage is already halfway a technomancer, some realize some don't.<br /> It would be sort of vulgar with witnesses(himself) to change the result.<br /> If the mage in question believes in chi imbalance, miasma, sickness spirits or even something completely alien for the rest of humanity, he also rationalized long ago, why a microscope shows what it shows. <br /> <br /> The only mage that wouldn't see pathogens and stuff wouldn't bring a microscope with him...<br /> <br /> Pretty convenient that timetravel is so close to suicide. So nobody volunteers to grab his microscope and do the science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:19:03-07:00","id":1196917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1196773#post1196773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simple answer is that the mage sees various pathogens. Because that is the reality he knows. A modern mage is already halfway a technomancer, some realize some don't.<br /> It would be sort of vulgar with witnesses(himself) to change the result.<br /> If the mage in question believes in chi imbalance, miasma, sickness spirits or even something completely alien for the rest of humanity, he also rationalized long ago, why a microscope shows what it shows.<br /> <br /> The only mage that wouldn't see pathogens and stuff wouldn't bring a microscope with him...<br /> <br /> Pretty convenient that timetravel is so close to suicide. So nobody volunteers to grab his microscope and do the science.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> its a sensory effect, how is it &quot;vulgar&quot;. I mean its basically &quot;life one&quot; people believe in the capacity of people to diagnose illnesses. So I don't see why it would be an issue at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:43:52-07:00","id":1196927,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I don't think you can do vulgar magic with yourself as a witness. If you don't believe the magic is possible, then how in the world would you cast it in the first place?<br /> <br /> Even sleepwalkers don't count as witnesses for their own magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:48:42-07:00","id":1196932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1196927#post1196927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... I don't think you can do vulgar magic with yourself as a witness. If you don't believe the magic is possible, then how in the world would you cast it in the first place?<br /> <br /> Even sleepwalkers don't count as witnesses for their own magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone uses Entropy 5 on you, they can erode your Faith in your own Magick. You become a Witness to everything you do, and it's all Vulgar. It's a nasty effect. But yeah that's a niche situation. It can even temporarily reduce your True Faith! Scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:27:57-07:00","id":1196969,"title":"","content":"Considering that Mages don't count as witnesses for other Mages' effects, that's an odd way of ruling a loss of faith. I could see the effect make a Mage unable to cast a spell, but not make the spell Vulgar. It may be in the books somewhere, but if so it's probably best to give it the same weight as much of HDYDT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:36:58-07:00","id":1196970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1196969#post1196969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Mages don't count as witnesses for other Mages' effects, that's an odd way of ruling a loss of faith. I could see the effect make a Mage unable to cast a spell, but not make the spell Vulgar. It may be in the books somewhere, but if so it's probably best to give it the same weight as much of HDYDT.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's in Core. The idea is that you've cut them off from their Paradigm. They can use Magick, but they are so sure it won't work they are essentially making themselves a source of Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T18:25:20-07:00","id":1196985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1196970#post1196970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's in Core. The idea is that you've cut them off from their Paradigm. They can use Magick, but they are so sure it won't work they are essentially making themselves a source of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, if they don't believe in what they are doing, they can't do any magic, so them being a witness to their own magic would be kinda irrelevant since they wouldn't be capable of doing the magic in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:34:11-07:00","id":1197141,"title":"","content":"I was a bit unclear in my wording, basically the mage would use magick to see illness in the sample by using the microscope as an instrument. To see something other he has to use a different instrument because it would be impossible for him to see something he doesn't believe via the microscope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:58:26-07:00","id":1197171,"title":"","content":"To put it another way, the way sensory spells impart information is highly related to paradigm. If an Akashic, a Chorister, and a Technocrat are diagnosing a TB victim, they will all make the correct diagnosis, but they will do so in different ways. The Akashic will recognize the specific energy imbalances related to the disease, the Chorister might be told by a messenger, and the Technocrat will find the presence of the appropriate bacteria. All three will see the fundamental information (that the victim is suffering from a wasting lung disease) but it will come clad in whatever way is appropriate to the spell (chi imbalance, messenger, or bacteria through a microscope).<br /> <br /> The microscope is so embedded in the modern world that most mages of this time can use one and see bacteria, and those versed in the sciences or medicine (even those without scientific paradigms) will be used to seeing results that are consistent with the results of their own magics. For a mage like that (say an Akashic with an MD) it is arguable that their familiarity with the modern paradigm is strong enough that they could use it as their actual paradigm if they went back in time. In that case they would see something consistent to what they were already used to, because the effect would impart information in a way consistent to its paradigm. <br /> <br /> If, instead, the time travelling mage was not well versed enough in the sciences or medicine they would be unable to use the microscope properly. They might find it hard to even focus the microscope, or to differentiate the blobs they were seeing through it. But they'd only get failure or something vaguely similar to what they would see in modern times, because people of the 1100s don't have any kind of opinion on what a microscope should show.<br /> <br /> The only mages who would see something drastically different through a microscope are those who already do. A very small subset of mages (mostly Etherites I think) might use modern equipment via very different scientific theories. That's an edge case though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:42:03-07:00","id":1198178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1194025#post1194025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is whether Miasma ever was a real thing. Back when most people thought &quot;foul vapours&quot; spread disease... did they spread disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for being obvious or/and pedant, but:<br /> <br /> Is it me or is this post really a discussion about B. Latour's book on Pasteur ?<br /> <br /> If a nutshell, if you say, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> , that miasma theory is absolutely wrong, and germ theory correct, you can presumably and logically only say that because you have a <a href=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/truth-correspondence/\" target=\"_blank\">correspondence theory of truth</a> - that is, you believe there is an objective reality out there. So your question isn't really a question, because you've already presumed the answer - by refusing to grant the possibility of a truthness (at least relative) to miasma theory. Now this is certainly something Latour would go great length arguing against you, because people who believed in miasma theory certainly thought they could &quot;see&quot; miasmas (and this belief, of course, had very real effects).<br /> <br /> So, to take your example, I assume they would probably see miasmas (but the time-traveller would probably see whatever he believes in). Today as yesterday, <i>people usually see just what they want to see</i> (I'm not sure you needn't enter heavy metaphysical-historical-sociological debates here...).<br /> <br /> <i>Sidenote</i>: the microscope probably isn't the best case for your point. In the Middle Ages, people would probably see &quot;<i>animalcules</i>&quot; (that is, tiny animals), just as they did in &quot;real history&quot; (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonie_van_Leeuwenhoek\" target=\"_blank\">Leeuwenhoek</a>'s term, for instance, for spermatozoids). Microscope was invented several centuries before Pasteur conceived the germ theory... (or, what is Microsoft?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23992-tazmaniacs","name":"Tazmaniacs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:49:58-07:00","id":1198183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1194025#post1194025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is whether Miasma ever was a real thing. Back when most people thought &quot;foul vapours&quot; spread disease... did they spread disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. Isn't this what smog does ;-) ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23992-tazmaniacs","name":"Tazmaniacs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:55:47-07:00","id":1198185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1193478#post1193478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An alternative suggestion: I don't think it would become a mere practice-tool that is dependant on the paradigm of the awakened/enlightend user. I think it would become a simple wonder!<br /> <br /> Since the microscope, upon traveling back in time, becomes something that has very defined abilities that are not part of the consentual reality it accordingly becomes full-blown sphere-magickal - as that is pretty much the definition of anything outside of full consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that any new &amp; surprising tech is vulgar (mostly Technocrat) magic? The Internet? DNA forensics ? Cinema yesterday - and still today, in some places. Etc. etc. How does the Technocracy copes with so much Paradox? <br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;IRL&quot;, people continually invented &amp; invent technologies which don't integrate in any scientific framework (but that's probably out of the point).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23992-tazmaniacs","name":"Tazmaniacs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T03:48:45-07:00","id":1198287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tazmaniacs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198183#post1198183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused. Isn't this what smog does ;-) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are obviously airborne pathogens and chemicals which can cause disease, but that wasn't the paradigm. The paradigm was that all illness was spread by &quot;foul air&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T04:12:29-07:00","id":1198292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tazmaniacs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198185#post1198185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean that any new &amp; surprising tech is vulgar (mostly Technocrat) magic? The Internet? DNA forensics ? Cinema yesterday - and still today, in some places. Etc. etc. How does the Technocracy copes with so much Paradox? <br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;IRL&quot;, people continually invented &amp; invent technologies which don't integrate in any scientific framework (but that's probably out of the point).</div> </div> </div> </div>With very good PR.<br /> <br /> Ever hear on the news about factory explosions and mass recall of items due to poison or overheating. Buildings collapsing or burning to the ground that were still fairly new? That\u2019s paradox.<br /> How about computer crashes, server failure and data corruption, or complete loss of files and records with no backup for years? That too is paradox.<br /> Examples of really big Technocract induced paradox backlash include Chernobyl and Fukushima, the stock market crash, and thalidomide induced birth defects.<br /> <br /> And each time the Union makes sure that if it can\u2019t be covered up, then at least it can be explained away. What\u2019s more is that each explanation that the masses accept is one step closer to turning their paradigm into consensus. So even in failure, their PR team can turn it into a win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-22-2018, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T04:19:01-07:00","id":1198293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198292#post1198292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With very good PR.<br /> <br /> Ever hear on the news about factory explosions and mass recall of items due to poison or overheating. Buildings collapsing or burning to the ground that were still fairly new? That\u2019s paradox.<br /> How about computer crashes, server failure and data corruption, or complete loss of files and records with no backup for years? That too is paradox.<br /> Examples of really big Technocract induced paradox backlash include Chernobyl and Fukushima, the stock market crash, and thalidomide induced birth defects.<br /> <br /> And each time the Union makes sure that if it can\u2019t be covered up, then at least it can be explained away. What\u2019s more is that each explanation that the masses accept is one step closer to turning their paradigm into consensus. So even in failure, their PR team can turn it into a win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Things going wrong is actually good for the paradigm in a way, since it shows trial and error and consistent progress, and invites MORE resources rather than less. We need to spend more money on research before releasing such drugs or building such factories, the public cry, hoping to be safe. And technocrats can rub their hands as the Quaternary sector of the global economy grows and grows and grows.<br /> <br /> Although one thing about Mage makes me a tad uncomfortable, and Werewolf does something similar. We risk straying into &quot;magical anti-vaxx&quot;, if you know what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T05:34:31-07:00","id":1198301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although one thing about Mage makes me a tad uncomfortable, and Werewolf does something similar. We risk straying into &quot;magical anti-vaxx&quot;, if you know what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a setting where literally all conspiracy theories have truth to them. There is literally a shadowy global government known as the New World Order. They literally have, or at least had, a base on the moon. Chemtrails are probably a real thing, as are spy satellites that could indeed be blocked by tin foil hats (corr. 2 rote with hat as focus, consensus enough to a conspiracy theorist sleeper)<br /> <br /> The Progenitors book even details how vaccines are the primary method by which they test new bodymorphoing drugs in the masses. You could even state that the whole autism caused by vaccines was a real thing in Mage, a paradox effect that has since been refined, with several Technocratic doctors trying their darnedest to cover it up, discredit it, or even dismiss it out right.<br /> <br /> Mage is a world of post truth. The technocracy understands the perils of this and are working hard to eliminate subjectivity to the consensus. However the cost is a policy of conform or die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-22-2018, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T11:28:47-07:00","id":1198368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198293#post1198293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Things going wrong is actually good for the paradigm in a way, since it shows trial and error and consistent progress, and invites MORE resources rather than less. We need to spend more money on research before releasing such drugs or building such factories, the public cry, hoping to be safe. And technocrats can rub their hands as the Quaternary sector of the global economy grows and grows and grows.<br /> <br /> Although one thing about Mage makes me a tad uncomfortable, and Werewolf does something similar. We risk straying into &quot;magical anti-vaxx&quot;, if you know what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, right? Take a game like D&amp;D that uses faith healing and there is no problem. But Mage says that vaccines didn't always work and that there are people ruthless enough to use them for unethical purposes and it gets uncomfortable. It's like an RPG uncanny valley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T14:35:22-07:00","id":1198408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198368#post1198368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny, right? Take a game like D&amp;D that uses faith healing and there is no problem. But Mage says that vaccines didn't always work and that there are people ruthless enough to use them for unethical purposes and it gets uncomfortable. It's like an RPG uncanny valley.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh 100%.<br /> <br /> True Faith healing people in a dark and fractured setting feels different to, basically all Cleric and Druid powers in softer settings. And then you gotta remember that Pentex's drug companies will be making Vaccines, and those will be spreading Wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> Are vaccines making your children into Fomori? 10 Reasons why you should be afraid!<br /> <br /> I guess that it's all fine, just with a small disclaimer. Like the old &quot;No you aren't a Vampire, no you can't follow a Path of Enlightenment, don't do illegal things&quot; disclaimers at the start of the VtM Revised books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:05:10-07:00","id":1198414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198368#post1198368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny, right? Take a game like D&amp;D that uses faith healing and there is no problem. But Mage says that vaccines didn't always work and that there are people ruthless enough to use them for unethical purposes and it gets uncomfortable. It's like an RPG uncanny valley.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find it funny that werewolf and mage is the uncanny valley when &quot;the Government is secretly Run by Vampires!&quot; is the foundational bit of the world of Darkness, with a heaping helping of &quot;the most common explanation of them is YEC!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:12:49-07:00","id":1198635,"title":"","content":"That's indeed, interesting. I take that as the consequence of Mage and Werewolf having compelling cosmologies that make people think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that it's all fine, just with a small disclaimer. Like the old &quot;No you aren't a Vampire, no you can't follow a Path of Enlightenment, don't do illegal things&quot; disclaimers at the start of the VtM Revised books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the firm opinion that people that can't discern between reality and fiction shouldn't play RPG. Ever. And that they should seek proffesional help.<br /> <br /> But yeah, totally. And if we go there Satyros warnings of not playing infernalists because it will really endanger your soul doesn't help.<br /> <br /> One big fat line has to be treaced between IOC and OOC and books have to be clear about it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh 100%.<br /> <br /> True Faith healing people in a dark and fractured setting feels different to, basically all Cleric and Druid powers in softer settings. And then you gotta remember that Pentex's drug companies will be making Vaccines, and those will be spreading Wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> Are vaccines making your children into Fomori? 10 Reasons why you should be afraid! </div> </div> </div>Or you could see things as Technocracy does and say that vaccines are one more step to finally get rid of sickness in the Consensus and anti-vax people are evil because by spreading doubt they effectively reduce the potency of the currently accepted way to heal people. A way that took hundreds of years of blood and tears to get into the Consensus.<br /> And for what?, no other option it's nearly Consensual enough to be as effective. They don't have a <i>real </i>plan, their actions are bound to kill as much or more inocent people than Pentex with their EDE's, and they do it just to satisfy their ego and get more power (and it's not like Pentex would stop introducing EDE's if vaccines are not around arround - they would just replace their Technephandi with regular Nephandi).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, there are many factions within the Traditions that would have strong opinions against any anti-vaxx mages for that very reason - it's part of the whole &quot;Traditions don't want to get back to the middle ages anymore&quot; plotline of Revised.<br /> <br /> Miasma theory failed because it was part of a world submerged in superstition. Consensus at that time was contested, and thus it hadn't enough weight to be super effective. It had to be culled because a new option wouldn't be related to the horrendous failures(Paradoxes) of those times. It took us hundreds of years to advance the populace up to the point they almost accept vaccines, creating an alternative not based on the framework of science would take another set of hundreds of years and manipulation. Doesn't that sounds as a good reason to use them even if they aren't ontologicaly self sufficient? (and yes, we know, the Syndicate really likes expensive fees, but that's not vaccines fault).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-23-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:29:34-07:00","id":1198824,"title":"","content":"As noble as that might be. The Progenitors still use vaccines as a vehicle for non consensual human testing of new life altering drugs and treatments. So yes the technocracy will yell \u201cgreater good\u201d, but one good concequence does not a justification make.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not too dissimilar to refusing to come forward about a time when an important political figure sexually molested you because the idea they represent is too powerful and important; with the good they might do too vital to risk ruining by discrediting their name.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s great and all, but they still sexually molested you and who knows who else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-23-2018, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T14:18:01-07:00","id":1198842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1193313-the-time-traveler-s-microscope?p=1198824#post1198824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As noble as that might be. The Progenitors still use vaccines as a vehicle for non consensual human testing of new life altering drugs and treatments. So yes the technocracy will yell \u201cgreater good\u201d, but one good concequence does not a justification make.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not too dissimilar to refusing to come forward about a time when an important political figure sexually molested you because the idea they represent is too powerful and important. With the good they might do too vital to risk ruining by discrediting their name.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s great and all, but they still sexually molested you and who knows who else.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL, doctors in the US sterilized native american women without their permission, without ever informing them. This was genocide, plain and simple, and it was done for what was considered &quot;the civic good&quot;. We have to remember that Eugenics were awesome and popular up until the fall of the 3rd Reich, at which point the public were put off scientific racism (somewhat, our governments gave total amnesty to practically every scientist involved with genocide because information is just worth too much). I mean even Churchill was a huge advocate for eugenics and scientific racism (and using chemical weapons on peaceful Iraqi tribal people, a suggestion which Conservatives in the early 1900s found ridiculously inhumane and racist). The real Churchill I mean, not the imaginary half-remembered man we got on the \u00a35 note. But I digress.<br /> <br /> So I think it's fair to say that the Technocracy has done the same kind of thing and worse, and that no one actually cares or remembers within the Technocracy itself. If the Technocracy were to be exposed and destroyed, THEN they'd be history's greatest monsters of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. This will include stuff surrounding vaccination, using it as mind-control or to test sterilizing agents or fertility agents, you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T14:43:29-07:00","id":1198848,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t say no one in the union cares. I think that the union has a lot of talk about conformity, and indeed a great number of methods to enforce conformity amongst its ranks, but I am sure there is actually quite a lot of diverse philosophies within the union itself.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say that in terms of strict adhearance to conformity, the hierarchy goes NWO &gt; Syndicate &gt; Iteration X &gt; Progenitors &gt; Void Engineers<br /> With the top being the convention which values conformity the most.<br /> <br /> However, that\u2019s not to say all NWO agents are thoughtless drones (even though some definitely are in a very literal sense), or that all Void Engineers are disparate free thinkers. But it is much more dangerous to be outspoken about your divergent thoughts within the NWO, and must be done through carefully chosen wording, closed doors, and plausible diniability.<br /> <br /> I do think of technocrats as incredibly human though. And with that comes differences of opinion, superiority dynamics, miscommunication, and all the joys of sweet and simple screwing up.<br /> <br /> Some progenitors might be less aware than others of the ethical pools their superiors intend to drown them in, others may be deeply troubled but ultimately too cowardly to challenge it. Others still may be very vocal about trying to find alternative methods, with varying degrees of flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T16:30:27-07:00","id":1198885,"title":"","content":"It is worth noting, given the themes of Mage, that most 'great' cultures are monstrous when you peel away their protective layer of historical lionization. Partly that's because of differences in views, ideologies, and priorities, partly because of disagreements over who counts as human, and partly because no culture ever lives up to its ideals. <br /> <br /> A fallen, exposed Technocracy would be the greatest of monsters, and it would be deserved. But it would also be deserved if they kept their principles, because in that case they could have done more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T02:09:24-07:00","id":1198984,"title":"","content":"At this point, a fallen technocracy would probably be the most dangerous event to befall human kind. Reality has become so reliant on them and the consensus so fortified, that their destruction would create chaos on a scale never imagined before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}